    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0020" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13897: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-13T20:00:00+08:00">January 13, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. The broadcast from Sian last night in English was made not by woman announcer
                    but by a man who spoke English with a Russian accent. He announced inaugural
                    meeting of new “National Salvation Association” on January 11, with 200
                    delegates, at which time pleas were made for a “war against traitors” and a
                    united front against Japan. The work of various propaganda agencies was
                    described. It was announced that “peaceful conditions” prevailed in Shensi and
                    Chiang Kai-shek was charged with “insincerity”.</p>
                <p>Captain Barrett<anchor n="23" xml:id="d7-f1"/> reports today from Loyang that the
                    military authorities at Loyang believe that the present difficulty will be
                    settled without resort to military force.</p>
                <p>By mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d7-f1" n="23" xml:id="d7-f1-content">
                <p>David D. Barrett. U.S.A., Assistant. Military Attaché in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
